---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/cof.css';

const title = 'Corrective Forcing: Unified Post-Training for Diffusions and Flows in Generative Speech Enhancement';
---

	<BaseLayout
		title={`${title} — Qing Yao`}
		description="Interactive demo for Corrective Forcing (CoF), unified post-training for diffusion and flow speech-enhancement models, with results on VoiceBank+DEMAND, WSJ0+WHAM, and WSJ0+REVERB."
		bodyClass="cof-body"
	>
	<main class="cof-page">
		<!--
			AGENT RESOURCE NOTE (intentionally hidden from rendered page visitors):
			This page currently ships as a ONE-SCREEN TEASER for the Corrective
			Forcing (CoF) speech-enhancement paper: hero (title/authors/links),
			the abstract rendered in full but masked by a white fade from its
			third line down (carrying the submission/demo note), and the Index
			Terms. The Overview,
			Benchmark Comparison, Quality-vs-NFE, Citation, References sections,
			and the footer are removed until the arXiv preprint is released; the
			chart islands (CoFBenchmarkBars, CoFNfeCurves) and src/data/cof.js
			were removed with them, so restoring the full demo means recovering
			those from git history as well. The paper's
			first-page footnote points readers of the CoF manuscript to this exact
			URL (https://yorch233.github.io/CoF).
			- Code repository: https://github.com/Yorch233/CoF/
		-->
		<article class="cof-article">
			<img class="cof-watermark" src="/logo/icon.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />

			<header class="cof-hero cof-fade cof-delay-1">
				<p class="cof-kicker">Paper Demo</p>
				<h1 class="cof-title">
					<span class="cof-highlight cof-title-method">Corrective Forcing</span>: Unified
					Post-Training for{' '}
					<br />
					Diffusions and Flows in{' '}
					<span class="cof-highlight">Generative Speech Enhancement</span>
				</h1>

				<p class="cof-authors">
					<span class="cof-author">
						<span class="cof-author-name">Qing Yao</span>
						<a class="cof-email" href="mailto:qyao@stmail.ujs.edu.cn">qyao@stmail.ujs.edu.cn</a>
					</span>
					<span class="cof-author">
						<span class="cof-author-name">Lijian Gao</span>
						<a class="cof-email" href="mailto:ljgao@ujs.edu.cn">ljgao@ujs.edu.cn</a>
					</span>
					<span class="cof-author">
						<span class="cof-author-name">Qirong Mao <sup class="cof-tag">†</sup></span>
						<a class="cof-email" href="mailto:mao_qr@ujs.edu.cn">mao_qr@ujs.edu.cn</a>
					</span>
				</p>

				<ul class="cof-affiliations">
					<li>Jiangsu University</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="cof-affiliation-note"><sup class="cof-tag">†</sup> Corresponding author</p>

				<div class="cof-links">
					<p class="cof-links-title">Links</p>
					<nav class="cof-nav" aria-label="Paper resources">
						<a
							class="cof-nav-link"
							href="https://github.com/Yorch233/CoF/"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noreferrer"
							aria-label="View source code on GitHub"
							title="GitHub"
						>
							<img class="cof-nav-icon" src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/github" alt="" />
							<span class="cof-nav-label">GitHub</span>
						</a>
						<span
							class="cof-nav-link is-disabled"
							data-disabled
							aria-disabled="true"
							title="arXiv preprint coming soon"
						>
							<img class="cof-nav-icon" src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/arxiv" alt="" />
							<span class="cof-nav-label">arXiv</span>
						</span>
					</nav>
				</div>
			</header>

			<section class="cof-section cof-section-separated cof-fade cof-delay-2 cof-teaser-base" aria-labelledby="cof-abstract-heading">
				<h2 id="cof-abstract-heading">
					<span class="cof-wave" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>
					Abstract
				</h2>
				<div class="cof-abstract-wrap">
					<p class="cof-abstract">
						<span class="cof-highlight">Diffusion and flow models</span> for speech enhancement face a{' '}
						<span class="cof-issue">training–inference mismatch</span>: training uses analytical path states,
						while inference operates on self-generated trajectories, where{' '}
						<span class="cof-issue">prediction and discretization errors accumulate</span>.
						We introduce <span class="cof-highlight">Corrective Forcing (CoF)</span>, a unified{' '}
						<span class="cof-highlight">post-training framework</span> that adapts models to these rollout states.
						CoF corrects clean-speech predictions toward the ground truth under varying sampling schedules
						and regularizes local transitions against locally corrected counterfactual references.
						A shared <span class="cof-highlight">clean-speech prediction parameterization</span> enables
						the same objective for diffusion and flow models. Experiments with SB-VE and OT-CFM on three
						benchmarks show gains in perceptual quality and reconstruction fidelity across sampling budgets.
					</p>
					<p class="cof-teaser-veil">
						<span class="cof-coming-soon"
							>This paper has been submitted to ICASSP 2027 and is under review. This
							demo is coming soon.</span
						>
					</p>
					<div class="cof-legend" aria-hidden="true">
						<span class="cof-legend-item">
							<span class="cof-legend-swatch cof-legend-swatch-highlight"></span>
							Key Concepts
						</span>
						<span class="cof-legend-item">
							<span class="cof-legend-swatch cof-legend-swatch-issue"></span>
							Challenges
						</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="cof-section cof-fade cof-delay-3" aria-labelledby="cof-keywords-heading">
				<h2 id="cof-keywords-heading">
					<span class="cof-wave" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>
					Index Terms
				</h2>
				<div class="cof-meta">
					<span class="cof-chip">Generative speech enhancement</span>
					<span class="cof-chip">Schrödinger bridge</span>
					<span class="cof-chip">Flow matching</span>
					<span class="cof-chip">Post-training methods</span>
					<span class="cof-chip">Exposure bias</span>
				</div>
			</section>

		</article>

	</main>
</BaseLayout>
